<title>POLAND: FORECAST- Polish banks see end-97 CPI at 14.96 pct.</title>
<headline>FORECAST- Polish banks see end-97 CPI at 14.96 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Inflation expectations among Polish banks fell for the second month running in May, a monthly Reuter poll of the 26 biggest banks showed on Monday.</p>
<p>Banks predicted average year-on-year inflation for the end of 1997 at 14.96 percent, down from 15.73 percent predicted last month but above the government's goal of 13 percent.</p>
<p>		   MAY	   END-97	  12-MONTHS AHEAD</p>
<p> CPI AVERAGE   0.93	14.96 (15.73)     13.55 (14.47)</p>
<p>     MINIMUM   0.4	 12.0  (14.0)	10.0  (12.5)</p>
<p>     MAXIMUM   1.3	 17.0  (17.5)	15.5  (16.7)</p>
<p>NOTE: In brackets previous figures for end-97 and April-98 from last month's poll.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
